Package: datparser
Title: Read Fixed-Width Text Files Through Their SAS Setup Files
Version: 3.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jonathan", "Bearak", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "jbearak@guttmacher.org")
Description: read_fixed_width() reads fixed-width .dat files, such as
    the National Survey of Family Growth's, through the SAS setup files
    that describe them: columns, variable labels, value labels, record
    selection and missing-value recodes. Columns come back as a tibble
    of standard R types, with value labels as attributes and the
    extended missing values .a to .z as tagged NAs. A small part of the
    dta-parser library, on its own; datakit includes it.
License: GPL-3
Depends: R (>= 4.2)
Imports:
    rlang,
    stats,
    tibble,
    tidyselect,
    utils
Suggests:
    haven,
    jsonlite,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc
Encoding: UTF-8
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
